.TH HTTP_CHUNK 3
.SH NAME
http_chunk \- queue a chunk of the body of a request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_chunk(http* " h ", const char* " x ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_chunk ()
encodes
.I n
bytes at
.I x
as one chunk (size in hexadecimal, CRLF, the data, CRLF) and appends it to the queued body of
the request. It calls
.BR http_chunked (3)
first if that was not done.
.P
It can be called before the request is sent, then the chunks go out right behind the headers,
and while it is being sent. In the second case the socket is registered for writing
and
.BR http_canwrite (3)
writes the chunk as far as the connection takes it. Data that is not written yet is kept, the
queue grows until the connection catches up.
.P
A chunk of length 0 is ignored, it would end the body; use
.BR http_chunk_end (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 on failure or if the body has ended.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_chunked(3), http_chunk_end(3), http_body_flush(3)
